WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.750
Full energy is troubled because there's no place to go

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.030
A slight shake destroys boredom

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.170
I Ride, On the White Line  OH, OH, OH

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.240
Sit Down  At the place I trust  OH, OH, OH

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.540
We can go even if we're lost

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.650
Everyone receives freedom and passion

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.850
We were born to shine, and our journey continues

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:56.060
Your soul is the key that supports our uncertain days

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.000
The best growth creates an unstoppable WILD DRIVE

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.270
We still quietly knock on the door

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.480
No way.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.200
It's huge!

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.500
It's monstrous.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.020
I was waiting for you, Seto.

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:34.440
Welcome, duelists.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:42.280
Well?  Will you duel us?

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.660
Wait a sec!

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:46.720
What happens if we lose?

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.390
Good question.

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:57.560
We'll switch places, and you'll wander through cyberspace for eternity!

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:58.800
No way!

00:01:58.800 --> 00:01:59.340
Damn!

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:00.570
That's not fair!

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.940
This is our revenge!

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:12.940
Deck Master Deepsea Warrior

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:31.480
If you defeat us, we'll release you from this virtual world.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:37.800
But if you refuse to duel, we won't let you leave this world.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:40.310
That's why you're garbage.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:42.470
I'll do it!

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.040
You'll face me first!

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.280
Brother!

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:55.800
Your friend's speech means you've all given your consent.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:00.130
Anzu!

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:02.590
Shizuka!

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:08.500
Big bro!

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.270
Kaiba!

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.070
The Big Five!  What will you do with them?

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.090
Big brother!

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:38.480
The Big Five!  How dare you do this!

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:49.950
What?

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:58.450
Where am I?

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.550
Where's my brother?

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.720
Why am I the only one here?

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:22.000
Otogi!  Are you okay?

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.970
Where are we?  Where's Shizuka?

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:37.590
Big brother!

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:43.300
Are you hurt?

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.020
I'm fine.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:53.340
Seto, you're my important guest.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:56.540
Enjoy this world for a while.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.290
Hey!  Shizuka!

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:24.800
The first duel is between Yugi Muto and the first of The Big Five, Deepsea Warrior.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.810
This is virtual reality?

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:32.600
I'm dueling here?

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:47.590
I'm your opponent.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:49.360
A monster!

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:57.370
As a loyal Kaiba Corporation employee, I took over and devoured many other companies.

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:04.170
My Deck Master, Deepsea Warrior, symbolizes my skills and abilities.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:08.110
In other words, I'm my own Deck Master.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:11.350
That's why you created the Deck Master System?

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:16.020
Yes.  We lost our bodies because of you.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:19.860
This is my temporary body so that I can get my revenge.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.510
Oh, one more thing.

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:26.860
If you underestimate this world because it's virtual, you'll pay dearly.

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:28.870
What do you mean?

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:30.650
You'll see.

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:34.050
I'll now get my revenge.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:37.870
I've had enough of this cyber world.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:40.800
I want to have a body.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:47.150
It'll be nice to relive my youth by taking over your young body.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:53.390
Your friends will soon meet my friends.

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:57.150
This is bad, partner.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.400
If they go after Anzu or Shizuka...

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:06.900
There's no reason for us to duel, but let's defeat him quickly and find Anzu!

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:11.010
We have to accept this duel.

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:21.520
I have no reason to get involved in your revenge plot, but let's get started.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.120
Bring it on!

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:26.860
Ooh.  You must be Yugi Type B.

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:28.360
What?

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:34.170
Yugi Muto, we've researched that you have two thought patterns.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:38.530
You're a duelist with two different minds.

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:41.280
Our research makes us prepared.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:46.380
“If you know your enemy and know yourself, you need not fear a hundred battles."

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:48.760
Let's start.

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:51.480
You can't use your deck in this world.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:53.920
You'll need to build a new deck.

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:55.170
What?

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:01.080
It's Kaiba Corporation's card data.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:05.430
Choose your cards by touching them.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:13.440
Who is this Noa who's backing up The Big Five?

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:19.640
Good.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.360
I've built my deck.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:26.150
Choose your Deck Master among your cards.

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:37.630
But I don't know what abilities each card has when it's a Deck Master.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.130
Gazelle...  Berfomet...

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.760
They won't work as a Deck Master.

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:45.400
I use Dark Magician often...

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:48.640
I'll go with Dark Magician.

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:56.260
Kuriboh!

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:58.980
You picked Kuriboh?

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:01.990
No!  Kuriboh appeared on its own!

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:07.820
Too bad.  You can't change your Deck Master once it's out.

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:08.900
What?

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.580
You're telling me to trust you?

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:16.070
Okay.  I'll trust you!

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:21.880
My Deck Master is Kuriboh!

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:28.080
As you can see, Deepsea Warrior is my Deck Master.

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.900
We're ready to begin.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:34.200
I'll show you how an adult duels!

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.960
The duel begins with my turn.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:45.660
I draw!

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:49.530
I summon a monster in defense position!

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:56.540
It's the first step in creating the formation I have in mind.

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:00.260
And it's also a clever trap.

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:02.050
I end my turn!

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:04.650
I was wondering what he'd try....

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:08.450
...but all he did was summon a monster in defense position.

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:12.050
But he definitely has a plan.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:21.300
According to my research, Yugi Type B will attack 80% of the time in this situation.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:26.550
Even if he suspects something, he won't change.  That will cost him.

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:33.580
I can't let him build his formation.

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:36.880
I will destroy his defending monster!

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:52.090
My turn!

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:53.030
I draw!

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:57.720
I summon Obnoxious Celtic Guard!

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.950
I set a card!

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:07.400
Let's battle!

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:11.280
Obnoxious Celtic Guard attacks your defending monster!

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:17.220
Good.

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:22.880
Just as I expected.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:24.790
Kids are so simple.

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:28.020
My Flip Effect activates!

00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:32.980
You must discard one card from your hand.

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:34.850
What?

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:45.310
When Ashingray is destroyed, I can summon another one from my deck in defense position.

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.550
Then I shuffle my deck.

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:52.420
How's that, Yugi Muto?

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:55.100
You destroyed my Ashingray, but it's back.

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:57.540
You didn't expect this strategy.

00:11:58.240 --> 00:11:59.530
I end my turn.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:03.600
How beautiful!

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.770
Such a nice breeze.

00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:17.080
Ahh!  Cold!

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:23.080
It looks pretty, but it's not real.

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:24.590
But...

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.970
The water does feel cold.

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:38.550
Brother...

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:42.870
Where am I?

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:48.150
I can't believe The Big Five showed up again.

00:12:48.150 --> 00:12:50.480
They can really hold a grudge.

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:56.040
The Big Five!  Show yourselves if you want to duel!

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:57.720
I don't have all day!

00:12:58.280 --> 00:13:00.260
I know you're watching!

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:01.590
Stop hiding!

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.020
Ignoring me?

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:15.110
I have to defeat Marik and save Mai as soon as possible!

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:16.600
You're here?

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:25.950
I don't have time to waste dueling you!

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.480
If you want to fight, let's fight!  Come out!

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:35.370
Shizuka!

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.770
Shizuka!  Where are you?

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:42.170
Damn.  We're lost inside a virtual maze.

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:44.500
The scenery never changes.

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:46.360
But...

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:47.920
What is it, Otogi?

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:51.660
Don't you think this virtual room is too big?

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:56.680
Who cares!  It's more important to find Shizuka!

00:13:56.680 --> 00:13:57.600
Let's go!

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:58.770
Hey!

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:05.740
This virtual world is well-made, big brother.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:12.630
It's more realistic than other virtual worlds, but it's still a copy of my Solid Vision.

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:16.400
Who is Noa?

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:24.560
He couldn't create this giant moving fortress or virtual system alone.

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:28.940
Neither could those Big Five losers.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:36.160
Someone with lots of money must be behind this to take over Kaiba Corporation.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:38.840
Can we escape this place?

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:40.200
Don't worry.

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:42.460
I know the basics of this system.

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:50.460
It's programmed to have an emergency exit in the shape of a window or a door.

00:14:57.490 --> 00:14:58.640
My turn.

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:00.470
I draw!

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:05.190
Ipiria.

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:10.720
If I summon Ipiria, I can draw a card from my deck.

00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:12.830
This is going well.

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:19.230
A political philosopher during the Italian Renaissance had three requirements to keep winning.

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:21.360
What's he talking about?

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:24.920
#1: Get a chance to win.

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:26.800
I summon Ipiria!

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:36.020
By summoning Ipiria, I get to draw a card.

00:15:36.020 --> 00:15:41.210
I switch Ashingray from facedown defense position to attack position!

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:48.300
Requirement to keep winning #2:

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:50.720
Possess skills.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:54.880
By changing formation, the Flip Effect activates.

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:58.730
You must discard one card from your hand.

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:00.470
Again!

00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:12.980
Ashingray has low attack points, but it's as good as a million soldiers when used correctly.

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:16.570
Both Ashingray and Ipiria have 500 attack points.

00:16:16.570 --> 00:16:18.690
Is he inviting me to attack?

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:25.820
We can't escape.

00:16:25.820 --> 00:16:28.630
At this rate, we can't save Shizuka!

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:33.050
I see!  There's no exit because this is a virtual world.

00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:35.600
So?

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:39.980
There's no exit because they never built an exit to begin with!

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:41.040
What?

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:43.110
Then we can never get out!

00:16:43.450 --> 00:16:45.110
That's correct.

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:47.110
Stop being depressed.

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:49.650
There's a simple fix.

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:51.670
If there's no exit, let's create one!

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:55.020
Break down the wall.

00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:56.570
I see!

00:16:56.570 --> 00:17:03.130
This may look like a castle wall, but it's probably a special screen.

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:06.870
We can go backstage if we destroy this wall.

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:08.800
But how?

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:14.040
That's not a virtual axe?

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:15.240
How can he hold it?

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:17.300
Take this!

00:17:30.720 --> 00:17:32.990
This is a virtual world too?

00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:36.720
Anyway, I have to find everyone.

00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:49.820
What?

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:54.810
I'm surrounded.

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:13.640
Help me, Yugi!

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:23.200
Big brother!  Look!

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:33.800
There's no mistake.

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:36.720
That's the Exodus Program, an emergency exit.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:51.470
Big brother...

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:53.120
That's...

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:57.810
We used to live in that facility.

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:00.170
How cruel...

00:19:00.170 --> 00:19:04.550
Why did Noa program this virtual world?

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:14.600
Does he want me to attack?  Or is he bluffing?

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:19.970
Damn.  He's dictating the pace, so I have to think more than usual.

00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:30.470
Kuriboh...

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:36.620
Whatever he's planning, I can't just do nothing.

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:40.690
My friends may be in danger!

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:42.190
My turn!

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:43.400
I draw!

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:45.090
Polymerization.

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:47.690
I'll end this at once!

00:19:48.970 --> 00:19:52.730
I fuse Berfomet and Gazelle the King of Mythical Beasts!

00:19:55.510 --> 00:19:56.970
Fusion Summon!

00:19:56.970 --> 00:19:59.340
Chimera the Flying Mythical Beast!

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:03.840
I activate the spell card Quick Attack!

00:20:04.940 --> 00:20:08.760
Chimera the Flying Mythical Beast attacks Ipiria!

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:13.020
Requirement to keep winning #3:

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:15.820
Lead the enemy to self-destruction.

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:17.340
I caught you.

00:20:17.340 --> 00:20:19.620
I activate my Deck Master's ability!

00:20:19.840 --> 00:20:21.630
Deck Master's ability?

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:25.130
My special ability is Reflector Hole.

00:20:25.170 --> 00:20:31.420
I tribute two monsters to send your monster's attack back to you!

00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:43.250
What?

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:54.640
How's that!

00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:57.360
This is my Deck Master's ability!

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:01.970
I now understand that this isn't a regular duel.

00:21:02.180 --> 00:21:03.800
Hurts, right?

00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:11.910
Your brain thinks that whatever happens in this virtual world is real, affecting your heart.

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:16.980
Your friends should be starting their duels in other areas.

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:23.690
Aren't you worried whether your friends can withstand the pain?

00:21:23.900 --> 00:21:27.000
We can't drag out this duel!

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:27.850
Yeah.

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:31.300
Let's defeat him quickly and go to our friends!

00:21:47.250 --> 00:21:53.220
No matter how many monsters Yugi defeats, Deepsea Warrior's combo keeps resurrecting them.

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:59.680
Meanwhile, Kaiba and Mokuba must face their past in another virtual world.

00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:04.450
Monsters are attacking Shizuka, and Hitotsu-Me Giant have captured me.

00:22:04.450 --> 00:22:06.620
Hurry and save us, Yugi!

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:09.710
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Terrifying Resurrection Combo

00:22:09.710 --> 00:22:11.170
Duel, standby!

00:22:13.650 --> 00:22:21.560
The sun never sets
It rises forever

00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:30.500
Don't let a dream end as a dream

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:35.470
The straight rail and harsh route

00:22:35.470 --> 00:22:39.440
Whether to go or not 
all of yourself

00:22:39.870 --> 00:22:47.410
I'm tired of counting on my fingers inside this cage

00:22:47.410 --> 00:22:50.980
Respect! Boys  Show me how you act tough

00:22:50.980 --> 00:22:55.750
Draw a map, even if it's sloppy

00:22:55.750 --> 00:23:05.860
And walk it without stopping

00:23:05.860 --> 00:23:13.470
The sun never sets
If I can be like you

00:23:13.700 --> 00:23:22.440
Create freedom by exceeding common ideas

00:23:22.440 --> 00:23:30.420
I want to trust myself
Sometimes I'll lose my way but

00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:40.260
I hide it in my heart...
Secret Paradise
